Z||000002||Will||07-07-2001||09:17 AM||||The Helm shop manual has some body schematics; enough to correct for collision damage, but I'm not sure if it's enough for your project, whatever that may be.<P>If you're going to be seriously modding your car, a real shop manual (NOT Haynes or Chiltons) is a necessity IMO.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Janson||07-07-2001||10:24 AM||||Thanks, G! I appreciate the welcome. ;-)<P>Well Will, I know this much: the roof of my car will undergo some serious structural changes - as will the shapes doors and the surrounding body. I've already done a few idea sketches. But sketches are no match for an accurate diagram and a work decent plan.<P>Thanks for the info. I'll check out Helm and see what they have. But do you have any idea on how to procure a real shop mannual?<P>------------------<BR>- Janson||||reg||1
Z||000004||Pontiaddict||07-08-2001||01:44 AM||||Here's a suggestion.<BR>Place some 4" strips of masking tape 4" apart down the centerline of the car. Take a picture of the car from far enough away to get the whole car in one shot.<BR>When you get the picture developed, get a copy blown up so that the strips in the picture are 1" and you'll have a 1/4 scale copy of the car to work with. (you could do this with a copy machine or on your computer if you wanted to) If you make extra copies of the 1/4 scale picture you can cut it apart and move the pieces around to get the look you want. The same technique could be applied to the space frame if you are just going to modify that and not use any of the original panels in your final plans.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Will||07-08-2001||07:47 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Janson:<BR><B>Thanks for the info. I'll check out Helm and see what they have. But do you have any idea on how to procure a real shop mannual?<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The Helm manuals <I>are</I> the real manuals.<BR>They handle GM's publishing. <A HREF="http://www.helminc.com" TARGET=_blank>www.helminc.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Janson||07-08-2001||09:59 PM||||Yeah, I figured that out as soon as I visited their site. It's just that you made it seem like Helms <I>wasn'</I> a real shop manual to beggin with.<P>I'm new to this, man. Bare with me. But thanks for the advice all the same.<P>------------------<BR>- Janson||||reg||1
